From: Brandon Payton <brandon@happycode.net>
Subject: [PATCH] swaybar: stop the text status reader at end of file

getline returns -1 at EOF without setting errno. The text reader tests
only errno, so an exited status command leaves it looping forever, with
a negative index into its buffer on subsequent iterations. An empty
command can also enter the text branch with read_bytes zero.

Guard the buffer index and close the status stream on genuine stdio EOF.
Nonblocking EAGAIN still clears the stream error and keeps it live.

This reproduces with the unmodified sway 1.12 reader on a native host;
it does not compensate for a Kandelo syscall or runtime limitation.
Source: https://github.com/swaywm/sway/blob/1.12/swaybar/status_line.c

diff --git a/swaybar/status_line.c b/swaybar/status_line.c
--- a/swaybar/status_line.c
+++ b/swaybar/status_line.c
@@ -106,12 +106,16 @@ bool status_handle_readable(struct status_line *status) {
 		// intentional fall-through
 	case PROTOCOL_TEXT:
 		while (true) {
-			if (status->buffer[read_bytes - 1] == '\n') {
+			if (read_bytes > 0 && status->buffer[read_bytes - 1] == '\n') {
 				status->buffer[read_bytes - 1] = '\0';
 			}
 			errno = 0;
 			read_bytes = getline(&status->buffer,
 					&status->buffer_size, status->read);
+			if (read_bytes < 0 && feof(status->read)) {
+				status_error(status, "[status command closed]");
+				return true;
+			}
 			if (errno == EAGAIN) {
 				clearerr(status->read);
 				return true;
